# Test Coverage Targets

RULE: `MIN_COVERAGE` in `scripts/quality-gates.sh` and `fail_under` in `pyproject.toml` must be set to **actual measured coverage - 1%**. Never leave it at the template default of 70% if actual coverage is higher.

WHY: Hardcoded 70% floor allows silent coverage regression from 95% down to 71% without any gate failure. Per-repo targets lock in current coverage and detect regression immediately.

## Required per-repo targets (update after intentional coverage improvements)

| Repo | MIN_COVERAGE |
|------|-------------|
| unified-events-interface | 99 |
| unified-internal-contracts | 99 |
| execution-algo-library | 95 |
| unified-feature-calculator-library | 93 |
| unified-ml-interface | 91 |
| unified-defi-execution-interface | 88 |
| matching-engine-library | 88 |
| unified-reference-data-interface | 87 |
| unified-config-interface | 77 |
| unified-sports-execution-interface | 73 |
| unified-trade-execution-interface | 72 |

## How to set coverage target

1. Run tests with coverage: `pytest tests/ --cov=<package> --cov-report=term-missing`
2. Note total coverage %
3. Set `MIN_COVERAGE = <actual> - 1` in `scripts/quality-gates.sh`
4. Set `fail_under = <actual> - 1` in `pyproject.toml [tool.coverage.report]`
5. Commit. Comment: `# Set to actual coverage - 1%. Update after intentional coverage improvements.`

DO:
- Set MIN_COVERAGE to actual - 1% after any significant coverage improvement
- Update the table above when targets change
- Review coverage targets during PR review to catch silent regressions

NEVER:
- Leave MIN_COVERAGE=70 if actual coverage is higher
- Lower MIN_COVERAGE without a documented reason in QUALITY_GATE_BYPASS_AUDIT.md
- Skip tests to pass the coverage gate
